  "chapter": {
    "number": 70,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(71) By David, a Psalm sung by the sons of Jonadab, and the first that were taken captive."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O Lord, I have hoped in you: let me never be put to shame.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "In your righteousness deliver me and rescue me: incline your ear to me, and save me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Be to me a protecting God, and a strong hold to save me: for you are my fortress and my refuge.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Deliver me, O my God, from the hand of the sinner, from the hand of the transgressor and unjust man.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For you are my support, O Lord; O Lord, you are my hope from my youth.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "On you have I been stayed from the womb: from the belly of my mother you are my protector: of you is my",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 126
          },
          {
            "text": "praise continually.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I am become as it were a wonder to many: but you are my strong helper.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let my mouth be filled with praise, that I may hymn your glory, and your majesty all the day.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Cast me not off at the time of old age; forsake me not when my strength fails.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For my enemies have spoken against me; and they that lay wait for my soul have taken counsel together,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "saying, God has forsaken him: persecute you⌃ and take him; for there is none to deliver him.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O God, go not far from me, O my God, draw near to my help.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let those that plot against my soul be ashamed and utterly fail: let those that seek my hurt be clothed with shame and dishonor.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But I will hope continually, and will praise you more and more.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "My mouth shall declare your righteousness openly, and your salvation all the day; for I am not acquainted with the affairs of men.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will go on in the might of the Lord: O Lord, I will make mention of your righteousness only.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O God, you have taught me from my youth, and until now will I declare your wonders;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 18,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "even until I am old and advanced in years. O God, forsake me not; until I shall have declared your arm to all the generation that is to come:",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 19,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "even your power and your righteousness, O God, up to the highest heavens, even the mighty works which you have done: O God, who is like to you?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 20,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "What afflictions many and sore have you showed me! yet you did turn and quicken me, and brought me again from the depths of the earth.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 21,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You did multiply your righteousness, and did turn and comfort me, and brought me again out of the depths of the earth.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 22,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will also therefore give thanks to you, O God, because of your truth, on an instrument of psalmody: I will sing psalms to you on the harp, O Holy One of Israel.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 23,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "My lips shall rejoice when I sing to you; and my soul, which you have redeemed.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 24,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Moreover also my tongue shall",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 127
          },
          {
            "text": "dwell all the day upon your righteousness; when they shall be ashamed and confounded that seek my hurt.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 126,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. hymn singing.",
